gosh seam 17: The core's programs are a domain, Frontend: its ABI at the top of src/frontend, its inside under imp/.

For:   REQ22/SHAPE-1, the core factored into domains by the seam, its programs last. The lint
       holds it (seam/DOMAINS): the rest of the core uses the programs only by terminaloverlay.h
       (the client's predictions; the core's benchmark). Until now the overlay was a namespace of
       its own, Overlay, whose header said `using namespace Terminal` and `using namespace
       Network` to every file that included it, and STMClient was in no namespace.
What:  Moves, and renames of where names are, and nothing else: no byte of the protocol, and no
       behaviour, changes. mosh-client.cc, mosh-server.cc, stmclient.* and terminaloverlay.cc are
       moved under src/frontend/imp/ by git's renames. Overlay is Frontend::Overlay; its header
       says Terminal:: and Network:: of the names it had used through those using-directives,
       and its source says them itself. STMClient is in Frontend::Imp. The two mains are where
       the language puts them, and as gosh's seam declares them (src/seam/core-main.h).
Where: src/frontend/ (Makefile.am, terminaloverlay.h; imp/); src/examples/benchmark.cc; configure.ac
       (AC_CONFIG_SRCDIR, the file by which configure knows the sources, names mosh-client.cc where it is).
Kind:  five files moved; the overlay's namespace, and STMClient's, changed; their users qualified.
From:  the core at the pin: src/frontend/{mosh-client.cc,mosh-server.cc,stmclient.cc,stmclient.h,terminaloverlay.cc}.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

